WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:05.990
I am the princess of the Star People, 
and I wandered here from outer space.

00:06.180 --> 00:07.620
<i>Princess?</i>

00:07.620 --> 00:09.500
<i>She might be dangerous...</i>

00:10.110 --> 00:15.070
Our customs dictate that a marital union be 
formed with the one linked by my stinger.

00:16.610 --> 00:20.280
Are those your family's customs?

00:20.280 --> 00:21.230
Yes.

00:21.660 --> 00:25.770
I was supposed to marry a 
partner of my parents' choosing.

00:26.820 --> 00:31.830
But I learned from manga how wonderful 
an unfettered love and life can be,

00:32.670 --> 00:35.160
and I decided to leave the island.

00:36.350 --> 00:41.230
And so Kuga-san, you and I must 
first attempt to fall in love.

00:41.480 --> 00:44.290
You don't want to obey 
those customs, do you?

00:44.290 --> 00:45.230
Correct.

00:45.660 --> 00:50.120
Then, is there any need to 
force yourself into love?

00:51.600 --> 00:56.530
I mean, falling in love is fine, 
but choose your partner carefully.

00:56.530 --> 00:57.630
I see your point.

00:58.420 --> 01:01.340
I do have the choice to not fall in love.

01:01.610 --> 01:05.620
Besides, it's always possible 
I already have someone.

01:06.070 --> 01:07.630
Do you?

01:07.630 --> 01:10.220
I don't at the moment.

01:10.220 --> 01:13.890
But let's just forget that 
whole thing. It's problematic.

01:14.370 --> 01:18.380
You've already been chosen, though.

01:22.140 --> 01:24.680
Oh, sorry. We'll come back to this.

01:24.680 --> 01:29.020
Um, would you mind if I got some rest?

01:29.780 --> 01:33.030
No problem. Feel free to take a nap.

01:38.500 --> 01:42.650
<i>What really is her deal?</i>

01:53.210 --> 02:00.510
Looks like it started before I knew it

02:01.260 --> 02:06.310
Thanks to you, I'm all smiles

02:08.230 --> 02:16.280
The usual townscape lends charm to the two of us

02:16.280 --> 02:21.780
Funny how it looks like a starry sky

02:25.540 --> 02:27.620
Suddenly buying flowers

02:27.620 --> 02:29.620
Standing around in the kitchen

02:29.620 --> 02:32.840
Sending a photo, because the setting sun is pretty

02:32.840 --> 02:37.380
Trying to spend as much time with you as I can

02:37.380 --> 02:40.380
This is all new for me

02:42.260 --> 02:47.930
I hope tomorrow is like today

02:48.270 --> 02:54.480
I've never felt this way before

02:54.480 --> 03:00.070
We'll go on a date this weekend if possible

03:00.740 --> 03:05.990
But it's fine if we stay home

03:07.240 --> 03:10.460
I can't wait to see you

03:12.960 --> 03:17.960
<b>Episode 2</b>

03:12.960 --> 03:17.960
<b>Shopping</b>

03:12.960 --> 03:17.960
<b>with the Princess</b>

03:18.500 --> 03:20.710
Hey, good work.

03:21.560 --> 03:22.590
What's wrong?

03:22.590 --> 03:24.590
I had a bit of a scare.

03:24.590 --> 03:27.570
I thought I was going to miss the deadline.

03:27.570 --> 03:29.130
Yeah, that'd be scary.

03:30.620 --> 03:34.350
Speaking of scary, I recently 
saw two horror flicks in a row.

03:34.350 --> 03:37.850
Oh, impressive. Were they any good?

03:38.280 --> 03:40.360
I think you could handle them, Kuga-kun.

03:40.670 --> 03:45.260
They both had to do with villages with 
strange festivals, customs, rituals, etc.

03:43.950 --> 03:46.370
customs

03:46.910 --> 03:48.680
No, I would pass.

03:48.680 --> 03:50.300
But they're entertaining.

03:52.610 --> 03:55.020
Oh, hey, why not draw some color pages?

03:55.020 --> 03:57.010
I like your coloring.

03:58.300 --> 03:59.500
Of course!

03:59.860 --> 04:02.250
Cool, take today off.

04:03.480 --> 04:04.750
Yes!

04:05.270 --> 04:07.480
My first color pages in a year!

04:21.110 --> 04:23.710
Good morning, everyone.

04:24.320 --> 04:26.070
Good morning, princess.

04:26.070 --> 04:27.160
Good morning.

04:40.340 --> 04:41.490
<i>Sure enough.</i>

04:43.930 --> 04:49.360
<i>I guess when I'm this far away from 
my people, our bond will weaken.</i>

04:53.890 --> 04:55.530
We're having barbecue tonight!

04:55.530 --> 04:56.910
Great.

04:56.910 --> 04:58.430
Where's Ichiro-kun?

04:58.430 --> 05:00.260
Still asleep, right?

05:02.060 --> 05:03.160
Excuse me.

05:04.200 --> 05:05.890
Goshiki-san, you're awake!

05:07.190 --> 05:08.740
Good morning.

05:08.740 --> 05:09.720
Um...

05:09.720 --> 05:13.220
Oh, I'm Chihiro Ibusuki from room 201.

05:14.890 --> 05:15.920
Chibi-chan!

05:17.420 --> 05:18.810
Good morning.

05:18.810 --> 05:21.420
Would you like to go get lunch?

05:21.420 --> 05:23.370
No, thank you.

05:23.370 --> 05:26.660
I'm going to head home first.

05:27.520 --> 05:28.370
All right.

05:33.280 --> 05:35.750
Ichiro, it's about dinnertime.

05:42.180 --> 05:44.200
He has a fever.

05:44.480 --> 05:46.690
You need to get decent sleep!

05:51.950 --> 05:54.450
I'd better text him where to send my pay.

05:55.370 --> 05:56.510
Text message.

05:56.510 --> 05:57.460
Who could it be?

05:57.460 --> 05:59.460
<b>bank info.txt</b>

05:57.460 --> 05:59.460
<b>Please send my payments to this bank account.</b>

05:58.210 --> 05:59.460
<b>I have a fever and will respond to you later.</b>

05:59.460 --> 06:02.220
Hey! Fumio, that's not your phone!

06:06.830 --> 06:08.230
Ichiro!

06:08.230 --> 06:11.470
Fumio! Get away, or you'll catch this!

06:14.920 --> 06:17.490
Get us sick! We'll split it into thirds!

06:18.100 --> 06:21.500
Chibi-chan, could you keep 
them isolated from me?

06:20.500 --> 06:21.960
Into thirds.

06:21.500 --> 06:22.540
S-Sure.

06:21.960 --> 06:23.860
Hurry and get better!

06:28.720 --> 06:32.610
<i>I'm so drained. Was this 
usually how colds feel?</i>

06:33.290 --> 06:35.720
<i>I wonder if Goshiki-san's all right.</i>

06:42.750 --> 06:45.760
Kuga-san, please hold my hand!

06:47.670 --> 06:52.630
I apologize for this, but it seems
 you're under my influence.

06:52.630 --> 06:56.750
Your fever appears to have formed because 
we moved away from each other physically.

06:57.390 --> 07:00.500
A fever because you and 
I got too far apart?

07:01.270 --> 07:05.140
Yes. It's more like my 
power than my influence.

07:05.140 --> 07:08.520
Do you feel a little better 
now that I've returned?

07:08.750 --> 07:12.020
Better than before, now that you mention it.

07:13.440 --> 07:14.750
I'm sorry.

07:15.290 --> 07:18.110
You're receiving retribution.

07:18.730 --> 07:22.770
For being my betrothed, 
yet being far apart from me.

07:23.790 --> 07:27.560
It's all to protect me, as princess.

07:27.560 --> 07:32.410
Neither I nor you can control the 
intentions of the Great Star.

07:33.780 --> 07:35.580
An accident may have led to this,

07:35.580 --> 07:39.080
but I never meant to put you 
through this unreasonable ordeal.

07:40.820 --> 07:42.120
I'm sorry.

07:43.780 --> 07:45.490
Hey, um...

07:45.490 --> 07:47.060
This whole scenario of yours?

07:47.460 --> 07:50.350
You don't need it either, do you?

07:50.350 --> 07:52.860
Oh, please don't get up.

07:55.480 --> 07:57.570
I'll lie down next to you.

08:06.950 --> 08:09.130
Y-You can get up!

08:09.130 --> 08:10.570
It's no problem.

08:10.570 --> 08:12.220
It seems awkward!

08:13.060 --> 08:19.570
Machi-san said you're doing work for your 
siblings' sake that isn't what you want to do.

08:19.980 --> 08:22.090
She said that?

08:22.090 --> 08:22.980
Yes.

08:22.980 --> 08:26.470
Well, it's true that I didn't have 
any luck with shonen magazines.

08:26.470 --> 08:29.890
And I was happy to be told that 
I'm cut out for shojo manga.

08:29.890 --> 08:32.360
But it's not only for 
Machi's and Fumio's sakes.

08:33.220 --> 08:34.850
Is that so?

08:35.160 --> 08:42.350
I'm just lucky that what I like to do and 
what I have to do happen to overlap.

08:42.860 --> 08:46.750
You accept your burden and 
search for the best path forward.

08:47.390 --> 08:50.010
I've never thought of it as a burden.

08:51.890 --> 08:57.130
Isn't it a tiresome idea that people need to 
be given things like burdens and retribution?

08:58.040 --> 09:01.720
Yes, I've long wondered if it's possible 
to share feelings with someone

09:01.720 --> 09:04.010
without controlling them!

09:04.490 --> 09:08.070
Like in those beautiful stories I've read.

09:12.010 --> 09:13.230
What's this?

09:14.600 --> 09:15.870
Rough color sketches.

09:15.870 --> 09:18.000
Color! It's been a year since you've done any.

09:18.000 --> 09:21.250
Yeah, I was so excited I drew a bunch.

09:23.470 --> 09:25.210
Which do you like best?

09:28.370 --> 09:30.380
I like this one.

09:30.380 --> 09:34.460
O-Okay, maybe I'll try expanding 
on this pattern a little more.

09:35.730 --> 09:37.380
Don't overdo it.

09:38.960 --> 09:42.140
Will I... get better if we hold hands?

09:42.140 --> 09:46.020
Physical contact should lessen the burden.

09:51.230 --> 09:53.410
I-If you would.

10:11.930 --> 10:13.290
<i>That's kinda comfy.</i>

10:13.820 --> 10:18.700
<i>I see. She's been telling 
the truth from the start.</i>

10:20.240 --> 10:22.890
<i>No matter how silly it might sound.</i>

10:38.820 --> 10:40.960
Fumio, where's Goshiki-san?

10:41.310 --> 10:42.510
Ichiro!

10:43.340 --> 10:46.010
Sorry about that. I'm fine now.

10:56.060 --> 10:58.890
Uh, about what you said.

11:00.090 --> 11:02.850
<b>Room for rent</b>

11:00.090 --> 11:02.850
<b>Now accepting tenants</b>

11:00.090 --> 11:02.850
Please feel free to inquire.

11:00.370 --> 11:01.830
This is lovely.

11:01.830 --> 11:02.520
Huh?

11:02.850 --> 11:09.600
<b>Now accepting tenants</b>

11:02.850 --> 11:09.600
Please feel free to inquire.

11:02.850 --> 11:09.600
<b>Room for rent</b>

11:03.200 --> 11:07.120
I'm still staying somewhere temporarily, 
so I'm looking for a place.

11:07.120 --> 11:09.290
Can I rent a room?

11:10.040 --> 11:13.620
As a friend, I recommend the place.

11:13.980 --> 11:17.600
Developing a relationship from 
friendship is lovely, too.

11:19.860 --> 11:20.990
<b>Hiiragi 
Apartments</b>

11:19.860 --> 11:23.160
Goshiki-san, you want to live here? Yay!

11:28.690 --> 11:30.470
Thank you for having me.

11:32.670 --> 11:36.130
<i>Goshiki-san moved in with 
very few belongings.</i>

11:36.960 --> 11:39.190
Yobijima, huh?

11:36.960 --> 11:39.840
Tenant's name: Shiori Goshiki
Current Address: Yobijima

11:39.830 --> 11:42.080
Princess of the Star People.

11:43.760 --> 11:46.650
How do I explain that to Machi and Fumio?

11:47.250 --> 11:48.270
Excuse me.

11:48.800 --> 11:50.350
I'll help out.

11:51.300 --> 11:54.870
No, it's okay. It's part 
of my landlord duties.

11:54.870 --> 11:57.610
Well, I also want to chat.

11:58.360 --> 12:01.580
Yeah, we do need to discuss 
what to do from here.

12:12.410 --> 12:18.260
You want to know if it's 
possible to annul our pact.

12:19.130 --> 12:20.260
<i>Is</i> it possible?

12:20.490 --> 12:26.290
I don't know yet, but I arranged for 
my staff on the island to look into it.

12:26.290 --> 12:28.760
Th-Thank you.

12:28.760 --> 12:30.310
Is that enough?

12:30.310 --> 12:31.270
That was quick!

12:31.270 --> 12:34.850
Th-Thanks. This helped me finish up early.

12:34.850 --> 12:35.770
No problem.

12:36.180 --> 12:38.780
I have a favor to ask of you, too.

12:38.780 --> 12:42.280
<i>Th-This timing makes it hard to refuse.</i>

12:42.840 --> 12:46.750
I want to go shopping. 
Could you come with me?

12:46.750 --> 12:48.170
Oh, is that all?

12:54.130 --> 12:57.320
Work clothes, everyday clothes, 
and daily necessities.

12:57.860 --> 12:59.540
Is it okay if I go look?

12:59.540 --> 13:00.560
Go ahead.

13:03.520 --> 13:08.510
<i>Machi still gets clothes from the children's 
section, so I never come to this floor.</i>

13:09.050 --> 13:10.390
Kuga-san, Kuga-san!

13:10.390 --> 13:11.800
Yes?

13:14.660 --> 13:16.320
What do you think?

13:19.180 --> 13:20.440
Either this...

13:21.310 --> 13:22.570
...this...

13:23.440 --> 13:25.090
...or this. I can't decide.

13:25.440 --> 13:29.020
I'm sorry, I can't tell the difference!

13:29.020 --> 13:31.450
I'll think on it a bit more, then.

13:32.950 --> 13:36.140
I-If I mix this in like this...

13:38.430 --> 13:39.760
What do you think?

13:40.450 --> 13:44.260
Well, it... looks like a school uniform.

13:44.260 --> 13:45.470
Does it?!

13:45.470 --> 13:47.050
Um...

13:47.700 --> 13:51.170
I guess nobody but students would wear this.

13:51.170 --> 13:52.480
Uh, no.

13:52.920 --> 13:55.730
It's fine for you to wear 
it because you like it.

13:55.730 --> 13:58.970
Did your school not have uniforms?

13:59.200 --> 14:01.770
They were correspondence 
courses, so no uniforms.

14:01.770 --> 14:04.470
I've always wanted to try wearing one.

14:05.210 --> 14:06.600
<i>Goshiki-san...</i>

14:06.990 --> 14:09.330
Then go on and buy it!

14:09.330 --> 14:11.500
I-I will!

14:14.980 --> 14:18.250
They have a lot more books than 
my grandmother's library!

14:18.680 --> 14:21.750
I-It's a gold mine! Wonderful!

14:22.050 --> 14:24.460
I might prefer some over others,

14:24.460 --> 14:28.000
but I suspect all the books out 
there in the world are interesting.

14:28.610 --> 14:30.520
I want to purchase one, for the occasion.

14:30.520 --> 14:32.900
Should I make it one of yours?

14:32.900 --> 14:35.010
No, don't worry about that.

14:36.880 --> 14:39.130
<i>She sure is straightforward.</i>

14:43.660 --> 14:45.510
I bought some!

14:45.510 --> 14:47.190
Good for you.

14:47.530 --> 14:49.160
Your custard pudding, miss.

14:49.540 --> 14:51.780
This is wonderful!

14:52.160 --> 14:54.280
Your strawberry brûlée parfait, sir.

14:55.220 --> 14:58.280
From me, to all the Star People.

15:02.170 --> 15:05.160
Are you... praying?

15:05.160 --> 15:08.090
No, it's a habit before eating.

15:08.090 --> 15:10.690
I thought I'd try connecting with my people.

15:10.690 --> 15:14.920
But maybe because of the 
distance, there's no response.

15:14.920 --> 15:18.510
Are you saying you can use 
telepathy with the islanders?

15:18.510 --> 15:20.570
It's something like that.

15:22.930 --> 15:25.020
Oh, my!

15:25.020 --> 15:26.940
This pudding is wonderful!

15:28.930 --> 15:31.930
Hey, I found the island's site.

15:31.930 --> 15:33.060
Site?

15:33.240 --> 15:35.080
Island legends

15:33.240 --> 15:35.080
Island life

15:33.240 --> 15:35.080
Sightseeing

15:33.240 --> 15:35.080
Access

15:33.540 --> 15:35.070
I mean this.

15:35.490 --> 15:38.160
There's so much I don't know.

15:38.580 --> 15:42.090
Hey, I never look at <i>my</i> local tourist sites.

15:42.090 --> 15:46.100
So, there's a page about 
legends told on the island.

15:47.310 --> 15:51.210
One day, the children of the 
island found a shooting star.

15:52.630 --> 15:58.340
The star fell at the foot of a 
mountain and began to cry and cry.

15:59.680 --> 16:04.450
A concerned island child came close, 
and the star's tears soaked into her.

16:04.450 --> 16:07.340
She could sense how sad 
the star was feeling.

16:08.750 --> 16:10.800
"I'm going to tell everyone else."

16:12.270 --> 16:15.310
She distributed the tears to other children,

16:15.310 --> 16:18.470
and they too could understand 
the star's feelings.

16:19.560 --> 16:22.200
It was so lonely, it couldn't stand it.

16:22.960 --> 16:28.360
For every tear the star shed, it grew smaller, 
and eventually disappeared altogether.

16:29.040 --> 16:30.350
But don't worry.

16:31.080 --> 16:36.640
The star's feelings got through to the 
people of the island, and it's not lonely anymore.

16:37.530 --> 16:42.800
Do the Star People you mentioned 
come from this story?

16:43.430 --> 16:46.510
It's been made easy for
 children to understand.

16:46.510 --> 16:50.240
I was taught it too, when I was little.

16:50.240 --> 16:52.390
It was a meteorite rather than a star,

16:52.390 --> 16:55.790
and I heard it brought with it 
some kind of microorganism.

16:56.070 --> 16:59.070
Doesn't that mean it's 
some kind of parasite?

16:59.070 --> 17:01.250
And that means, you...

17:01.250 --> 17:04.790
According to my grandmother,
 it's coexistence rather than parasitism.

17:05.030 --> 17:08.420
She was the first Star Child, 
two generations before me.

17:09.070 --> 17:14.050
I never had any deep conversations 
with her when I was young,

17:14.650 --> 17:17.180
A year ago, when my mother's rule began,

17:17.180 --> 17:20.330
my grandmother started teaching me stories.

17:20.690 --> 17:22.190
I see.

17:22.190 --> 17:27.700
They were exciting for me, as until then, 
I'd only had limited contact with books.

17:28.390 --> 17:32.210
History filled with revolutions, 
everyday activity in foreign lands...

17:33.100 --> 17:36.400
Huge schools, with tyrannical 
student councils.

17:36.400 --> 17:38.630
The amusing fellows who stand up to them!

17:38.630 --> 17:39.440
Huh?

17:39.440 --> 17:44.450
The fire in my heart blazed up, 
and before I knew it I was copying away!

17:44.450 --> 17:47.850
Uh, what's your grandmother doing now?

17:48.290 --> 17:49.830
She passed away.

17:50.410 --> 17:51.830
Oh.

17:51.830 --> 17:54.330
Mother was against me leaving the island,

17:54.330 --> 17:57.960
but it was my grandmother who supported it.

17:58.680 --> 18:03.570
Then it must be hard for you 
that I have to stick close,

18:03.570 --> 18:05.590
now that you've finally managed to leave home.

18:07.540 --> 18:12.190
Just so you know, the reason 
I'm looking into how to annul the pact

18:12.190 --> 18:15.610
is not because I'm dissatisfied with you.

18:15.990 --> 18:19.020
If I desire a genuine romance with you,

18:19.020 --> 18:22.030
would I really have wanted it 
to be based on an accident?

18:22.630 --> 18:26.870
It's therefore important to me to be sincere

18:26.870 --> 18:29.370
as we move forward with 
proper marital relations.

18:29.370 --> 18:33.440
Well, it doesn't have to be 
me if we annul the pact!

18:33.440 --> 18:35.620
We'll find someone else good for you!

18:43.000 --> 18:45.020
Sorry, I suddenly...

18:45.020 --> 18:46.560
I'll go wash my hands!

18:49.830 --> 18:52.020
<i>That was a surprise!</i>

18:52.020 --> 18:54.550
<i>You never know </i>what<i> she'll say.</i>

18:55.030 --> 18:56.900
Sure, I love manga.

18:55.760 --> 18:57.030
That's great!

18:57.830 --> 18:59.020
Kuga-san.

19:00.230 --> 19:03.900
These two said they wanted 
to talk about manga.

19:03.900 --> 19:06.660
This must be one of those 
so-called offline gatherings!

19:06.660 --> 19:07.900
No, it's not!

19:08.240 --> 19:10.670
Hey, let's at least exchange contact info.

19:10.670 --> 19:11.910
What's your name?

19:11.910 --> 19:13.170
Let's go.

19:13.170 --> 19:14.120
Ow!

19:16.680 --> 19:18.850
Kuga-san, let go of my hand!

19:26.220 --> 19:27.380
Kuga-san!

19:27.950 --> 19:28.720
Blood?

19:29.250 --> 19:30.970
Are you all right?

19:30.970 --> 19:31.990
I am.

19:33.380 --> 19:34.990
Shall we go?

19:34.990 --> 19:36.000
Yes.

19:36.480 --> 19:38.970
<b>Neyasu Shrine</b>

19:36.480 --> 19:38.970
<b>Neyasu Shrine</b>

19:38.980 --> 19:42.650
Uh, it's stopped and I'm fine now.

19:42.650 --> 19:44.990
Sorry to worry you.

19:45.350 --> 19:47.180
Please don't apologize.

19:47.180 --> 19:51.490
I was the cause of both the 
sneeze and the nosebleed.

19:52.560 --> 19:54.760
Fevers aren't the only thing?

19:55.390 --> 19:58.150
The retribution for unwelcome

19:58.150 --> 20:02.270
forceful contact manifests as 
a range of physical maladies.

20:02.270 --> 20:06.120
But it was to get you away 
from those sketchy guys.

20:06.610 --> 20:09.460
I never meant to cause you harm.

20:10.010 --> 20:13.170
I didn't understand that.

20:13.800 --> 20:19.240
And because of that, I hurt you.

20:20.030 --> 20:24.540
If I hadn't left the island, 
this never would have happened.

20:25.530 --> 20:26.790
Goshiki-san!

20:27.620 --> 20:31.810
You had never even drawn 
manga before, right?

20:31.810 --> 20:32.600
Right.

20:33.270 --> 20:35.660
If you became that good in such a short time,

20:37.280 --> 20:39.930
you must have practiced a heck of a lot.

20:40.380 --> 20:44.070
You were able to work at it that 
hard because you enjoy it, right?

20:44.070 --> 20:44.880
Yes.

20:45.620 --> 20:51.970
Then don't say you wish you hadn't 
done it because of someone else.

20:54.770 --> 20:58.200
Why are you crying?

21:00.190 --> 21:02.090
I-I'm not crying!

21:02.090 --> 21:03.500
But...

21:03.500 --> 21:05.570
May I touch you, then?

21:14.070 --> 21:15.130
See?

21:17.310 --> 21:19.210
<i>Oh, my sinuses cleared.</i>

21:19.530 --> 21:22.440
Thank you for being considerate.

21:23.710 --> 21:29.790
I do... want you to find out 
how to annul the engagement.

21:29.790 --> 21:30.710
Right.

21:31.040 --> 21:34.480
But if you're going to live here,
 I want to help you.

21:35.230 --> 21:38.220
I'll learn the rules of being with you.

21:38.570 --> 21:40.260
O-Okay.

21:48.230 --> 21:49.750
Why are you embarrassed?

21:49.750 --> 21:52.500
I've never worn pants before.

21:52.500 --> 21:57.260
You two must be getting along well, 
though, if you went shopping together.

21:57.260 --> 21:59.260
They did?

21:59.260 --> 22:00.690
Stop that, Machi.

22:00.690 --> 22:01.740
It's true!

22:01.740 --> 22:05.630
I was glad when he said he 
wanted to know more about me.

22:08.300 --> 22:10.890
Maybe I should have kept that our secret?

22:12.380 --> 22:14.510
I-Ichiro?!

22:16.060 --> 22:27.650
A long red thread stretching into the distance

22:27.650 --> 22:38.800
Meeting you, even if it meant having to cross hundreds of light-years

22:38.800 --> 22:45.480
Maybe I'll slowly get used to

22:45.480 --> 22:52.390
The two of us going out to have fun

22:52.390 --> 23:02.230
A tug on my arm, by the bond that was formed that day

23:02.230 --> 23:08.090
A little at a time, we've come closer together

23:08.090 --> 23:12.880
More smiles for us

23:12.880 --> 23:25.690
That place I first learned of, and the shops we'll visit again tomorrow

23:25.690 --> 23:31.650
They'll all be part of these lovely days

23:31.650 --> 23:38.490
Looking forward to it, good night

23:46.800 --> 23:48.190
Do you know about romance?

23:48.190 --> 23:49.140
Rome-ants?

23:49.140 --> 23:52.190
They say your heart races, 
and you get all jealous!

23:52.190 --> 23:53.520
Jell-us?

23:53.520 --> 23:56.320
There's always room for jell-us!

23:55.910 --> 23:59.900
<b>Episode 3</b>

23:55.910 --> 23:59.900
<b>Drama Bomb with the Princess</b>

23:56.320 --> 23:57.650
Moka-nee!
